// Cyrus v6: the UNIVERSAL mod categories (PURE, client-safe, no runtime imports).
//
// One canonical set, identical for every game, used by the studio map (game -> category -> mod),
// the prompt router (lib/cyrus/route.ts), the post-forge listing dialog, the NxLabs mod store and
// the per-game GameSupport files (lib/cyrus/games/<id>.ts `categories`). Ids are stable: they are
// stored on projects (ModBuild.cyrus.category) and in store filters, so never rename one; add a
// new id instead and map the old one in LEGACY.
//
// The template generators (lib/cyrus/engine) still think in their twelve ARCHETYPES
// (`CategoryKey` in lib/cyrus/types.ts). `engineCategory()` maps a universal id to the archetype
// that generator should use, so the generators did not have to change.
//
// The AUTO-SORTER (`autoSort`) classifies a finished mod into one primary + up to two secondary
// categories from deterministic signals only (zero API calls): the prompt, the title/summary,
// the build's commands/permissions/config and the generated code's API calls. When the signals
// are weak it says so (`confident: false`) and the listing dialog asks the owner to confirm; it
// never guesses silently and never calls a model.

